IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://houstonarboretum.o
 rg/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Green-Tree-Frog-on-leaf.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://houstonarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2
 026/04/Green-Tree-Frog-on-leaf.jpg
UID:qCJtxnMsb-l3J5tb62Dc1
SUMMARY:Froggy Night
DTSTAMP:20260808T091832Z
DTSTART:20260815T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:$37 member / $52 nonmemberInstructor: Dr. Cassidy Johnson Ages 
	21+ \n\n\n\nHop on over for a wet\, wild night! Enjoy refreshments (frog-t
	hemed snacks\, coffee\, and Saint Arnold Brewing Company beer) while you l
	earn all about the strange and wonderful world of frogs\, from their croak
	ing courtship to their mysterious metamorphosis. Weather permitting\, we’l
	l also go for a hike to search for frogs and other nocturnal creatures. \n
	\n\n\nPlease dress for the weather and wear walking shoes. \n\n\n\n\nregis
	ter online\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nInstructor bio: Dr. Cassidy Johnson has a B.S.
	 and M.S. in Biology at Texas A&M University – Corpus Christi and a Ph.D. 
	in Biochemistry & Cell Biology from Rice University. She loves teaching bi
	ology and is currently an Assistant Teaching Professor for Rice BioScience
	s. She fell in love with local amphibians while working for the Houston to
	ad ex situ conservation program at the Houston Zoo. She is also passionate
	 about the protection and restoration of Texas prairies and is on the boar
	d of the Native Prairie Association of Texas and was previously the presid
	ent of the Coastal Prairie Partnership.\n\nhttps://houstonarboretum.org/ev
	ent/froggy-night/\n\nFrom Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
URL:https://houstonarboretum.org/event/froggy-night/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:houston-arboretum
CATEGORIES:Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
