UID:HjbJD3BzZ2-wQGS0inFXR
SUMMARY:Park Conversations: Remembering and Honoring the Soldiers of the 3r
	d Battalion\, 24th Infantry Regiment
DTSTAMP:20260808T091832Z
DTSTART:20260820T080000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a free audio story exhibit at Clay Family Eastern G
	lades\nBeginning August 20\, Memorial Park Conservancy and the Buffalo Sol
	diers National Museum invite the public to Clay Family Eastern Glades for 
	the annual return of our historic interactive audio installation\, Park Co
	nversations: Remembering and Honoring the Soldiers of the 3rd Battalion\, 
	24th Infantry Regiment. The exhibit will be available to experience on-sit
	e through September 27. \nCan’t make it to the exhibit? All stories are av
	ailable online. Click Here to learn more and listen now. \nThe history of 
	Memorial Park and Camp Logan\nBefore Memorial Park\, the land was Camp Log
	an – a U.S. Army training camp built in the spring of 1917\, just weeks af
	ter the United States entered World War I. That summer\, African American 
	soldiers of the 3rd Battalion\, 24th Infantry Regiment\, one of the Army’s
	 four “Buffalo Soldiers” regiments\, arrived to guard the camp’s construct
	ion. \nIn the aftermath of the tragedy on August 23\, 1917\, the battalion
	 was disarmed and transferred. What followed was the largest court-martial
	 in American military history\, resulting in the execution of 19 soldiers 
	and life sentences for 63 others. \nThat verdict stood until November 13\,
	 2023\, when the U.S. Army formally set aside the convictions of all 110 s
	oldierstried in the case. The Army also committed to correcting the soldie
	rs’ service records\, making their descendants eligible for benefits their
	 families had been denied for a century. \n  \nExhibit Details:\nPresented
	 in partnership with the Buffalo Soldiers National Museum\, the installati
	on uses onsite audio stories to bring this history to life throughout Clay
	 Family Eastern Glades. \n\nWhere: Clay Family Eastern Glades\, 552 East M
	emorial Loop Drive\, Houston\, TX 77007\nWhen: August 20 – September 27\nC
	ost: Free and open to the public\nBring headphones. The audio is designed 
	for personal\, uninterrupted listening\nParking: Paid parking available on
	site at a rate of $2 for 3 hours. Free parking is available in adjacent lo
	ts.\n\nhttps://www.memorialparkconservancy.org/event/park-conversations-re
	membering-and-honoring-the-soldiers-of-the-3rd-battalion-24th-infantry-reg
	iment-2/\n\nFrom Memorial Park Conservancy
URL:https://www.memorialparkconservancy.org/event/park-conversations-rememb
	ering-and-honoring-the-soldiers-of-the-3rd-battalion-24th-infantry-regimen
	t-2/
LOCATION:Clay Family Eastern Glades\, 6500 Memorial Dr\, Houston\, TX\, 770
	07\, United States
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:memorial-park-conservancy
CATEGORIES:Memorial Park Conservancy
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT921H
END:VEVENT
